<%#
  SAVED CALCULATIONS (2026-10-21; plan 2026-10-21-calculator-modal.md): results saved from the
  calculator modal's Save to project, oldest first, each with its label, the expression and the
  answer. ON DEMAND (ProjectsController::ON_DEMAND): absent while empty, offered by "+ Add panel",
  and quiet when opened that way — its heading, the button that opens the calculator, and one line
  saying how a row gets here, because the calculator is the only way in.

  NEVER PUBLIC. public/projects/_page's `public_panels` map is the whole definition of a public
  face, and this key is not in it, so neither a visitor's page nor the owner's preview renders it.

  Reads @project, @calculations and @panel_layout, like the panels around it. The rows are their own
  partial so CalculationsController#create's stream can replace them when a save from the modal
  lands while this page is open.
%>
<section class="panel calculations-panel<%= " panel--quiet" if @calculations.empty? %>" id="project-calculations">
  <div class="panel-head">
    <h2><%= panel_title(@panel_layout, "calculations") %></h2>
    <button type="button" class="btn small" data-calculator-open aria-haspopup="dialog"
            title="Open calculator (<%= calculator_shortcut %>)" aria-keyshortcuts="<%= CalculationsHelper::CALCULATOR_KEYS %>">Open calculator</button>
  </div>
  <%= panel_intro(@panel_layout, "calculations") %>
  <%= render "projects/calculation_rows", project: @project, calculations: @calculations %>
</section>
